504 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The time gap between these two solutions can be attributed to the difference in their complexities. The Schwarzschild solution can be derived in a straightforward process just using basic analysis and is covered in almost all courses on general relativity worldwide. On the other hand, the derivation of the Kerr solution requires detailed knowledge of algebraically special metrics and deals with solving the Cartan structure equations. It is orders higher in complexity. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [12]
>>
