/E (Intercalated structures take a different approach by inserting foreign atoms or molecules between layers of a host material. This is similar to placing spacers between books on a shelf, changing the spacing and interactions among adjacent layers. For example, inserting lithium ions between layers of graphite creates lithium-intercalated graphite, which is now the standard anode in lithium-ion batteries. It hosts lithium ions between its carbon layers to store energy. In a similar vein, calcium-intercalated graphene shows potential as a high-temperature superconductor, and copper ions between MoS2 layers can improve catalytic activity for hydrogen production.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
endobj
