/E (Prof. Nirmal Raj, from the Centre for High Energy Physics at IISc Bengaluru, works at the intersection of particle physics, astrophysics, and cosmology, focusing on understanding dark matter and hidden sector physics. His research explores theoretical models for dark matter and develops strategies to detect them through experiments, astrophysical observations, and extreme environments like neutron stars. By combining theory with innovative detection methods, his work aims to expand the ways we can probe the unseen components of the universe.)
/Pg 46 0 R
